  "text": {
    "en": {
      "text": "Grants 20% increased damage for 16 seconds upon activating both <arc/>Arc and <stasis/>Stasis Overcharge one after another.\n\nNo time limit between the two activations.",
      "updatedAt": "2026-01-16T20:37:26.976Z",
      "updatedBy": "Stardust"
    }
  },
  "associated": [],
  "compendium": {
    "gid": "441434520",
    "rowKey": "Graviton Spike\n\nTemporal Manipulation I–IV\nTemporal Anomaly\n↑Craftable Traits",
    "section": "Energy Slot Weapons",
    "snapshot": {
      "plain": "Craftable Arc + Stasis Modal Hand Cannon\n[Reload] to swap between 150RPM Arc Firing Mode and 95RPM Stasis Firing Mode, refilling 3 Ammo.\n\nScoring a combined total of 3 Kills and Precision Hits within 7 seconds of each grants Overcharge to the opposite element.\nOvercharge progress persists through stow and reload, but is cleared upon swapping firing modes.\nOvercharge begins passively draining at a rate of -4.5% per second upon fully charging, even while stowed. \n\n150RPM Arc Mode:\nFires bullets that deal 141 [42.03] Damage with a 1.85x Precision Multiplier.\n\nArc Overcharge:\nKills and Precision Hits call down a lightning strike, dealing up to 262, down to 0% damage over 2 meters + 240 over 5 meters = 502 [21 + 21 = 42] Arc Damage.\nEach Precision Hit consumes 34% (-7s) Arc Overcharge. Hitting Stasis Crystals will consume 34% (-7s) Arc Overcharge to call down a lightning strike on them.\n\n95RPM Stasis Mode:\nFires explosive bullets that deal 185 [43.2] Impact Damage and up to 149 [21.02] Explosive Damage, down to 0% damage over 3 meters with a 1.85x Precision Multiplier.\n\nStasis Overcharge:\n Kills and Precision Hits trigger a Stasis Explosion that deals up to 126 [?] Damage, down to 0% damage over 7 meters and create 2 seekers perpendicular to the target.\nSeekers spawn a Medium Stasis Crystal rotated 45 degrees away from the enemy after traveling 4 meters, forming a \\  / shape.\nEach Precision Hit consumes 34% (-7s) Stasis Overcharge.\n\n↑Catalyst grants multiple craftable traits:\nTemporal Alignment Refit grants 20% [?%] increased damage for 15.5 seconds upon triggering both Arc and Stasis overcharge within 7 seconds of each. \nTriggering the buff has no time limit, and the buff can be refreshed by overcharging both modes in the same order it was activated in.\nOther options include the Rapid Hit trait, the Subsistence trait, and the Transcendent Moment trait.",
